title: helmepponye_confess
location: ballroom
---

Well, you took your shot and it didn’t quite work out. That was disappointing, but you suppose there’s always next year. As midnight approaches, you refresh your drink and try to get into the mood again, but it’s hard. 
You’re standing alone near the door when a voice interrupts your circling thoughts.
Helmeppo: Hey {$name}, you busy?
You look up to see him smiling at you. He’s wearing one heck of a purple suit and has left his signature visor at home for this event.
As he looks down at you, the smile fades a little.
Helmeppo: Hey. Something wrong?
-> No, I’m fine.
    He raises an eyebrow.
    Helmeppo: If you say so, I won’t pry.
-> Actually, yeah. It hasn’t been a great night.
    He nods sympathetically.
    Helmeppo: Sorry to hear it. 
Helmeppo: Mind if I try to distract you for a bit, then? 
{$name}: Be my guest.
He moves to stand next to you. You both lean on the wall, watching the party.
Helmeppo: I needed a bit of a break. Fighting pirates has nothing on forced socialization.
{$name}: I can see that. The intrigue. The back and forth.
Helmeppo: A true battle worthy of the Marines.
Comfortable silence falls between you.
Helmeppo: But anyway, I’m glad I found you. I wanted to tell you something.
{$name}: Oh? What?
You glance over to see… Is he blushing?
Helmeppo: I meet a lot of new people in the Marines. I don’t usually find myself thinking about them much. But my thoughts keep returning to you.
He’s *definitely* blushing now.
Helmeppo: I think I like you. And tonight seemed like a night for sharing secrets. So I figured, why not be honest?
-> Actually, I feel the same.
    Helmeppo: You do?
    {$name}: Yes. Do you need a lesson on when things *aren’t* jokes?
    He looks surprised, but it dissolves into a broad, natural smile almost immediately. Around you, the crowd begins counting down to midnight.
    Helmeppo: Wow. Just in time, it seems.
    {$name}: Seems like.
    As midnight hits, the two of you share your first kiss. Maybe this wasn’t what you were hoping for. But right now, it feels perfect.
    <<jump helmepponye_end>>
-> I’m sorry. I don’t feel the same.
    He takes in a breath, holds it a moment, then lets it all out.
    Helmeppo: I didn’t think so. But I wanted to say it. Happy New Year, {$name}. 
    He smiles sadly and walks away, leaving you with your thoughts.
    <<jump helmepponye_end>>
===

